# {{projectName}}

This is a generated TinyGres TypeScript/Vite starter.

- Work in `client/` and run `npm run dev` there.
- TinyGres owns its {{#if usesOpfs}}OPFS-backed{{else}}in-memory{{/if}}
  page-native database and Rust/WASM engine inside a dedicated Worker.
- Keep the database standalone and local. External services belong in separate
  application code.
- Await `create()`, use parameterized `query()` calls, use parameter-free
  `exec()` scripts, and call `close()` during teardown.
- Run related schema DDL in one atomic `exec()` bootstrap. Use
  `transaction(callback)` for related parameterized `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, and
  `DELETE` work, and keep the transaction object inside its callback.
- Preserve the three-table many-to-many query, aggregate summary,
  subscription-driven re-query, and visible revision/error state when changing
  the demo.
{{#if usesOpfs}}
- Preserve the stable `{{storageName}}` OPFS name and idempotent schema/seed
  setup so reloads do not replace existing data.
{{/if}}
- Keep SQL within TinyGres's documented compatibility contract and validate
  changes with `npm run build`.
